import{_ as t,o,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 246 | Realm Comparison · Cover the Sky: Realm Inflation and Setting Collapse","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 246 | Realm Comparison · Cover the Sky: Realm Inflation and Setting Collapse","no":246,"module":1,"tags":["Realm Comparison","Cover the Sky","Realm Inflation","Setting Collapse"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise","244-Realm and Future Infinite Expandability","17-Plane Transcendent Standards"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0246_模块1-境界对比-遮天体系境界膨胀与设定崩坏.md","filePath":"en/0246_模块1-境界对比-遮天体系境界膨胀与设定崩坏.md"}'),i={name:"en/0246_模块1-境界对比-遮天体系境界膨胀与设定崩坏.md"};function r(s,e,l,u,d,c){return o(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-246-realm-comparison-·-cover-the-sky-realm-inflation-and-setting-collapse" tabindex="-1">Entry 246 | Realm Comparison · Cover the Sky: Realm Inflation and Setting Collapse <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-246-realm-comparison-·-cover-the-sky-realm-inflation-and-setting-collapse" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 246 | Realm Comparison · Cover the Sky: Realm Inflation and Setting Collapse&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 1 · In-Depth Realm Refinement | Baseline references: Documents 04, 244, 17</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-infinite-inflation-from-great-emperor-to-mortal-world-immortal" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Infinite inflation from &quot;Great Emperor&quot; to &quot;Mortal-World Immortal&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-infinite-inflation-from-great-emperor-to-mortal-world-immortal" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Infinite inflation from &quot;Great Emperor&quot; to &quot;Mortal-World Immortal&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou (Wanling Hengmao Origin Cosmos)&#39;s realm system is rooted in law self-consistency, while Cover the Sky&#39;s realm system is characterized by &quot;continuous inflation&quot; — from the early &quot;Great Emperor&quot; to the late &quot;Mortal-World Immortal,&quot; realm names continuously increase, power numbers continuously inflate, early settings are continuously overturned. This inflation is not &quot;natural growth,&quot; but typical manifestation of <strong>plot kidnapping setting</strong>.</p><p>The six top-level axioms run through the comparison throughout: the anti-predation axiom points out Cover the Sky&#39;s predatory essence; the republican axiom of Myriad Races contrasts Cover the Sky&#39;s oligarchic structure; the collective ascension axiom contrasts Cover the Sky&#39;s solitary immortal ascension; the causal self-discipline axiom contrasts Cover the Sky&#39;s history falsification; the law-first axiom directly points to Cover the Sky&#39;s setting self-consistency collapse; the universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-cover-the-sky-s-realm-inflation-trajectory" tabindex="-1">I. Cover the Sky&#39;s Realm Inflation Trajectory <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-cover-the-sky-s-realm-inflation-trajectory" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Cover the Sky&#39;s Realm Inflation Trajectory&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Cover the Sky trilogy (Cover the Sky, Perfect World, Sacred Ruins)&#39;s realm system has undergone multiple inflations:</p><ul><li><strong>Cover the Sky arc</strong>: Great Emperor as ceiling, &quot;Mortal-World Immortal&quot; as hidden tier</li><li><strong>Perfect World</strong>: from immortal to Immortal Emperor, realm count doubles</li><li><strong>Sacred Ruins</strong>: stacking new realms further above, above Immortal Emperor there are even higher tiers</li><li><strong>Cross-book linkage</strong>: different books&#39; realms cross-reference, continuously breaking old ceilings</li></ul><p>This inflation&#39;s result is: readers cannot remember how many realms there are; early characters&#39; strength positioning repeatedly changes; settings contradict themselves.</p><h2 id="ii-three-manifestations-of-realm-inflation" tabindex="-1">II. Three Manifestations of Realm Inflation <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-three-manifestations-of-realm-inflation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Three Manifestations of Realm Inflation&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_2-1-name-inflation" tabindex="-1">2.1 Name Inflation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-1-name-inflation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.1 Name Inflation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Every segment of plot needs new realm names, otherwise the protagonist&#39;s growth &quot;is not worth watching.&quot; From &quot;Quasi-Emperor&quot; to &quot;Great Emperor&quot; to &quot;Mortal-World Immortal&quot; to &quot;Immortal King&quot; to &quot;Immortal Emperor&quot;... names get bigger, but actual law connotation gets emptier.</p><h3 id="_2-2-number-inflation" tabindex="-1">2.2 Number Inflation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-2-number-inflation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.2 Number Inflation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Early setting &quot;Great Emperor&quot; is the cosmos&#39;s strongest, one Great Emperor can suppress an era. Late &quot;Great Emperor&quot; becomes cannon fodder, below Immortal Emperor all are ants. Number inflation&#39;s result is early &quot;strongest&quot; becomes late &quot;weakest,&quot; readers feel deceived.</p><h3 id="_2-3-setting-contradiction" tabindex="-1">2.3 Setting Contradiction <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-3-setting-contradiction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.3 Setting Contradiction&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Early-set &quot;ultimate law&quot; late becomes basic law; early &quot;cosmos&#39;s unique&quot; becomes &quot;one of parallel cosmoses.&quot; To let the protagonist continue getting stronger, early settings are continuously overturned — this is retcon.</p><h2 id="iii-cover-the-sky-s-energy-level-waste-analysis" tabindex="-1">III. Cover the Sky&#39;s Energy-Level Waste Analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-cover-the-sky-s-energy-level-waste-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Cover the Sky&#39;s Energy-Level Waste Analysis&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Protagonist waste</strong>: Ye Fan from mortal to Heavenly Emperor, all the way predatory leveling, massive defeated opponents&#39; energy wasted</li><li><strong>Supporting-character waste</strong>: early vivid characters late become background boards, their settings and storylines wasted</li><li><strong>Setting waste</strong>: early carefully designed law system overturned in late inflation, front-loaded setting resources wasted</li><li><strong>Civilization waste</strong>: Cover the Sky&#39;s cosmos civilizations are continuously &quot;harvested,&quot; one era&#39;s civilization results reduced to ashes after strong ones predate them</li></ul><h2 id="iv-cover-the-sky-s-protagonist-uniqueness-dependency" tabindex="-1">IV. Cover the Sky&#39;s Protagonist Uniqueness Dependency <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-cover-the-sky-s-protagonist-uniqueness-dependency" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Cover the Sky&#39;s Protagonist Uniqueness Dependency&quot;">​</a></h2><p>By the five-level standard, Cover the Sky&#39;s protagonist uniqueness dependency is <strong>medium (Ye Fan / oligarch type)</strong> — Ye Fan as protagonist is indeed civilization&#39;s apex, but Cover the Sky also has other Great Emperor-tier figures, not completely solitary-tree type. But overall, civilization&#39;s core progress revolves around the protagonist; supporting characters are more &quot;running mates.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">V. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Assessment Dimension</th><th>Cover the Sky Score</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Realm self-consistency</td><td>Low</td><td>Realm definitions continuously change with plot needs, front-back contradiction</td></tr><tr><td>Retcon risk</td><td>Extreme</td><td>The trilogy continuously breaks previous works&#39; settings, retcon is normal</td></tr><tr><td>Ending risk</td><td>Medium-high</td><td>After cross-book linkage settings are overly complex, hard to self-consistently conclude</td></tr><tr><td>Plot kidnapping setting</td><td>Extremely severe</td><td>Protagonist&#39;s need to get stronger is the sole driver of realm inflation</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Core problem</strong>: Cover the Sky&#39;s realm inflation is not &quot;laws naturally expanding,&quot; but the vicious cycle of &quot;plot needs stronger enemies → needs stronger protagonist → needs higher realm.&quot; Law definitions completely obey plot needs, this is typical plot kidnapping setting.</p><h2 id="vi-heng-yuan-zhou-s-alternative-solution" tabindex="-1">VI. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Alternative Solution <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-heng-yuan-zhou-s-alternative-solution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Alternative Solution&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How does Heng Yuan Zhou avoid realm inflation?</p><ul><li><strong>Law-first</strong>: realm definitions precede plot, not modified due to plot needs</li><li><strong>Dimensional leap</strong>: every realm corresponds to an existence dimension, not number inflation</li><li><strong>Infinite expandability but self-consistent</strong>: new realm additions based on new law dimension discoveries, not to make the protagonist stronger</li><li><strong>Myriad Races group</strong>: strong ones are a group not individuals, no &quot;protagonist must be strongest&quot; plot pressure</li></ul><h2 id="vii-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">VII. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#vii-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VII. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Universal infinite backstop</strong>: the universal equal infinite law establishes that every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing have a guarantee, strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose, predation naturally loses meaning</li><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: Cover the Sky&#39;s realm inflation causes massive front-loaded setting waste; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s every realm is effective accumulation, not overturned and restarted</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: Cover the Sky&#39;s leveling is essentially predatory — fight strong enemies, seize energy; Heng Yuan Zhou replaces predation with symbiotic circulation</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo is ceiling lock, Cover the Sky is infinite inflation — both are problems, Heng Yuan Zhou takes the middle road</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Cover the Sky&#39;s strong ones are concentrated in the protagonist and few supporting characters; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s 20% Activation Strategy lets all Myriad Races have opportunity</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s expansion is based on law self-consistency, Cover the Sky&#39;s inflation is based on plot needs</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Cover the Sky&#39;s realm inflation is essentially &quot;continuously breaking self-set ceilings to let the protagonist keep winning.&quot; Short-term very satisfying — protagonist gets stronger, battles get bigger; long-term is disaster — settings continuously collapse, reader trust consumed. Heng Yuan Zhou starting from the law-first axiom lets the realm system be based on law structure not plot needs, rooting out inflation and collapse from the source.</p><p>In the final analysis, realm comparison · Cover the Sky realm inflation and setting collapse described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise</a> · <a href="./244-境界与未来-衡元宙境界体系的无限扩容性.html">244-Realm and Future Infinite Expandability</a> · <a href="./17-位面至高强者标准.html">17-Plane Transcendent Standards</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',33)])])}const g=t(i,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
